  "full_chain_findings": [
    "Actual registered EntityRaccoon installs wash goal2, dropped-item target selector1 and chest looting7. Native Mob dispatches server-only effective AI, target selector before goal selector; non-every-tick wash increments are goal updates, not a guaranteed100/20 world tick clock. WrappedGoal delegates and running-state stop is conditional. No runtime executed.",
    "Dropped target selection requires empty hand, eligible edible-or-foodstuff-tag stack, age>0 and mount guards. Default radius9 cube around mob+0.5; sorted by distance, not guaranteed reachable/visible. At squared distance<2 the consumer calls onGetItem before shrinking original stack1. No native playerTouch/target-owner/pickup-delay/onItemPickup hook in this custom path; getOwner resolves Thrower in current ServerLevel, not NBT Owner pickup target. A null/unloaded thrower supplies no taming UUID. Empty ItemEntity is discarded on native tick only if its item-update hook does not early-return; not an immediate discard receipt.",
    "Raccoon callback copies exactly one item (tag/caps copied by ItemStack.copy), sets100 search timer and captures thrower UUID only for tameable tag; overwrite/drop request of old hand and BlueJay teaming alternate branch occur before debit. Team branch can consume incoming food without retaining duplicate. Callback does not itself debit ground stack, caller does. Separate chest path copies1 then shrinks chosen container stack; ten search ticks, no thrower refresh. Container mutation/save atomicity and all teaming behavior not certified.",
    "Wash canUse requires nonempty hand plus positive search timer and chooses the LAST qualifying of15 random xz offsets[-16,15] starting y+3, scanning down through empty blocks to min height. Water needs one cardinal neighbor with empty fluids at body/head; it does NOT test dry neighbor solid ground or empty collision. targetPos is the first fluid-empty neighbor, used as continuation token, while navigation actually requests WATER coordinates. No guaranteed standable bank/path/reachability.",
    "Start extends timer1800. Continuation requires hand nonempty, target token, not in water and current food predicate; does not recheck water/land validity or timer/path. Within squared distance<=1 to water center, stop movement, set wash/syncedpos and timer0, then increment local washTime. Distance>2 resets wash flag without resetting accumulated time; leaving close range pauses updates. Terminal normal>100 or dissolving-tag>20 calls stop FIRST (clears pos/time/wash and sets search100), then optionally requests heal10/eat event, then postWash, crafting-remnant drop request and shrink1. Dissolving branch suppresses heal/eat but still reaches postWash/remnant/debit. No material conversion item or guaranteed loot is produced.",
    "Parent native heal is Forge-hooked and conditional on positive result/alive HP; call does not guarantee10 health gained. Server entity fallback decrements search timer; when expired and not washing plus eligible hand, it requests eat/remnant/debit with NO postWash taming callback. Timer1800 is not canContinue timeout; an unreachable running goal and fallback scheduling cannot be called an assured timed abort.",
    "PostWash requires current tameable-tag food, nonnull stored thrower and not already tame; RNG<.3 setsTame thenOwnerUUID and optional online-server-player advancement, then event7, else6. This code uses setters rather than tame(player) or an explicit onAnimalTame cancellation hook. Native setters modify synced data; owner save/load from TamableAnimal checked. Client superclass consumes6/7 as particle requests; final rendered visuals and network receipt are not certified.",
    "Entity additional NBT saves command/sitting/carpet/stealCooldown, not eggThrowerUUID, search timer, wash flag/pos or goal local washTime. Native Mob handItems NBT is separate and can preserve held food while transient wash/thrower context resets for a newly loaded instance. No claim existing-instance read clears absent fields, full migration safety, duplication exploit or actual save execution.",
    "Chest raid config/griefing/tame guards and villager-theft branch were read as surrounding acquisition context, not extra credit. Chest random chooses nextInt(size-1) when>1, excluding last selected slot; raw stack shrink and no explicit inventory.setChanged in shown raid is not a proven persistence defect. Existing custody may leave stored thrower context unchanged on non-ground paths. PostWash has no per-item provenance token proving captured UUID still belongs to current held food. No runtime exploit alleged.",
    "Mod sitting override writes separate SITTING synced field while native orderedToSit private field/isOrderedToSit have own storage. This contextual observation is not a new immunity fix or separate credit. Shared navigation, taming, packet, tags, config, sounds, carpet and offspring paths count0 additional.",
    "getOwner on ground ItemEntity returns any currently resolved thrower Entity, not necessarily Player. postWash stores its UUID as tamable owner even if player lookup fails; native OwnableEntity.getOwner resolves players only. No claim every accepted thrower produces an actionable player-owned companion."
  ],
